Căutăm un AML Analyst pentru a se alătura unei echipe specializate în prevenirea și combaterea spălării banilor și a finanțării terorismului.
În acest rol vei analiza alerte și tranzacții atipice, vei investiga activitatea clienților și vei evalua riscurile din perspectiva AML/FT, contribuind la respectarea cerințelor de conformitate și a procedurilor interne.

Responsabilități
• Analizarea alertelor generate de instrumentele AML/FT și efectuarea investigațiilor necesare asupra conturilor și activității clienților;
• Identificarea și analizarea tranzacțiilor atipice și evaluarea riscurilor asociate din perspectiva AML/FT;
• Documentarea analizelor efectuate și formularea opiniilor privind închiderea alertelor sau escaladarea acestora pentru investigații suplimentare;
• Gestionarea solicitărilor și cererilor de opinie primite din partea structurilor interne responsabile de AML;
• Solicitarea și analizarea informațiilor suplimentare necesare pentru soluționarea cazurilor;
• Colaborarea cu echipele și structurile interne relevante în gestionarea alertelor și investigațiilor AML;
• Contribuția la îmbunătățirea continuă a proceselor și instrumentelor de detectare a riscurilor AML/FT;
• Respectarea procedurilor interne și a reglementărilor aplicabile în domeniul prevenirii spălării banilor și combaterii finanțării terorismului;
• Redactarea analizelor și documentației specifice în limba franceză și/sau engleză.

Cerințe
• Experiență în domeniul AML / Financial Crime / Compliance / KYC, preferabil în sectorul financiar-bancar;
• Cunoștințe privind reglementările și principiile aplicabile în domeniul AML/CTF;
• Experiența în analiza alertelor, tranzacțiilor sau investigațiilor AML constituie un avantaj important;
• Capacitate foarte bună de analiză, sinteză și atenție la detalii;
• Capacitatea de a identifica riscuri și de a formula concluzii argumentate;
• Foarte bune abilități de comunicare scrisă și verbală;
• Limba franceză – min B2;
• Cunoștințe bune de Microsoft Office, în special Word și Excel;
• Capacitate de organizare, autonomie și respectarea strictă a confidențialității informațiilor;
• Studii superioare, preferabil în domeniul financiar-bancar, economic, juridic sau într-un domeniu relevant.

Ce oferim
• Pachet de beneficii și condiții de lucru competitive;
• Oportunitatea de a lucra într-un mediu profesional, într-o echipă specializată în domeniul AML / Financial Crime;
• Posibilitatea de a-ți dezvolta experiența într-un domeniu cu expunere internațională;

2d0f17491417.description:
Short company description

 Who we are?

We are Grant Thornton. We go beyond business as usual, so you can too. Grant Thornton Romania was founded in December 2010. During this period, our company has been continuously committed to providing quality and value services to clients. We are dedicated to serving the needs of privately held business and public interest companies delivering assurance, tax and advisory services. We approach all assignments by combining excellent consultancy services and dedicated, professional staff with experience at both local and international level. Over the last three years we are the fastest growing large accounting organization and we are constantly evolving and developing alongside our clients. Grant Thornton International is one of the world’s leading organizations of independent assurance, tax and advisory firms. With more than 80,000 Grant Thornton people, across over 150 countries, we are focused on making a difference to clients, colleagues and the communities in which we live and work.

What do we value?

We are a young team of professionals who have in common the Grant Thornton core values: Collaboration, Agility, Respect, Excellence

Here at Grant Thornton, we like to think big!

 Requirements

We are seeking an experienced AML/KYC Compliance Officer to take a key operational role within our compliance team, working with the support of a junior colleague. The successful candidate will bring hands-on AML/KYC experience gained within a Romanian reporting entity and will be expected to perform customer due diligence in practice, assess client risks, maintain complete AML/KYC files and support compliance with the obligations applicable under Romanian AML legislation.

The position offers the opportunity to play a central role in the day-to-day operation of the AML/KYC function, interact directly with senior stakeholders and help shape practical compliance processes within a professional services environment.

You will work directly with client-facing and support teams to apply AML/KYC requirements at client acceptance and throughout the business relationship. The position requires someone who can assess files critically, identify missing or inconsistent information, request relevant supporting documents, record well-reasoned conclusions and escalate higher-risk cases appropriately.

Qualifications and experience:

Bachelor’s degree in Law or Economics; specialized AML/KYC or compliance training is an advantage;

At least 3 years of experience specifically in AML/KYC or compliance, preferably gained within a Romanian reporting entity, such as an audit, accounting, tax, legal or financial services organisation;

Practical knowledge of Romanian AML/CTF requirements, including Law no. 129/2019, customer due diligence, identification of beneficial owners, risk classification, ongoing monitoring, record-keeping and the internal escalation of potential suspicious activity;

Experience reviewing corporate documents, ownership and control structures, beneficial ownership information, source-of-funds documentation, sanctions screening and politically exposed person screening results for client acceptance and ongoing review;

Ability to identify gaps or inconsistencies in AML/KYC files, request appropriate supporting documentation, record a clear rationale and escalate higher-risk matters;

Fluency in Romanian and English, both written and spoken;

Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook;

Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain document requests and compliance conclusions to colleagues and senior stakeholders;

Ability to manage several reviews and follow-ups at the same time, maintain complete records and meet internal or statutory deadlines;

Good judgement, professional skepticism and attention to detail when reviewing information that may be incomplete, inconsistent or commercially sensitive

 Responsibilities

 Key responsibilities:

Perform and document AML/KYC reviews for new and existing clients, including identification and verification, beneficial ownership analysis, assessment of the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship, risk classification and enhanced due diligence where required;

Review corporate and ownership documents, screening results and source-of-funds or source-of-wealth information; identify gaps, inconsistencies and risk indicators and follow up until the file supports a documented decision;

Support the maintenance and practical application of the company’s AML/CTF policies, risk methodology, client acceptance procedures, registers and internal controls in line with Romanian legal and regulatory requirements;

Monitor due dates for periodic reviews and changes affecting client risk; update KYC records and ensure that supporting documentation and approvals are complete and traceable;

Advise engagement teams on AML/KYC requirements, review higher-risk cases and escalate indicators of potential suspicious activity or other material compliance concerns through the company’s internal reporting channels;

Develop and deliver practical AML/CTF training and awareness sessions for client-facing and support teams, including updates on Romanian legal requirements, internal procedures and recurring issues identified during file reviews; contribute to compliance monitoring and the preparation of information required for internal reviews, and external inspections. 

 Other info

 What We Offer:

Competitive salary package and performance bonus;

Flexible benefits package within an allocated monthly budget;

Hybrid working model;

Private healthcare subscription, with the option to include family members at preferential rates, as well as accident insurance;

Support for professional development, including coverage of costs associated with relevant certifications (ACCA and/or others), in line with internal policies;

Additional annual leave days, in line with internal policies;

If you are looking for a role where your experience is valued and your contribution has a real impact on the success of our projects and team, we invite you to join us. 

 Benefits 

 • 
 Performance bonus 

 • 
 Medical subscription 

 • 
 Trainings 

 • 
 Courses 

 • 
 Choose your benefits within a maximum budget 

 • 
 Extra days off 

 • 
 Teambuildings / trips 

 • 
 Parties / company events 

 • 
 Meal vouchers 

 • 
 Holiday vouchers 

 • 
 Cultural vouchers 

 • 
 Gift vouchers

