We’re always looking for the ones truly passionate about their work. If you are amongst them, you can rest assured there is a place for you in eMAG. We’ve grown very fast and are determined to keep doing so. What brought us here is our desire for continuous evolution and practical results.

More than 6000 colleagues are part of eMAG Teams. We strongly believe in people's development and therefore every year we invest more and more energy and resources to remain an organization that is constantly learning. We want to ensure that you’ll have the most talented colleagues and the proper environment to grow and achieve great results, to become what you desire on a personal and professional level. Join us, grow faster!

Head of Legal & Compliance @HeyBlu

Our Mission: HeyBlu is a Romanian e-money licensed fintech company that aims to provide financial services to customers and merchants operating in the e-commerce space. Our vision is to increase the financial power of e-commerce buyers & sellers, making a positive impact in their everyday lives. We do this by extending the purchasing power of retail shoppers in easy and convenient ways, while also helping e-commerce merchants with the capital needed to grow their business.

Being part of eMAG group, the largest e-commerce player in Romania, HeyBlu is focusing on building a financial offering for customers and merchants operating within the eMAG ecosystem by implementing an “embedded finance” approach. As part of the global Prosus group, we share the same purpose: “Improving everyday life for billions of people through technology”. In the HeyBlu team we are building an entrepreneurial, results-driven, agile, and collaborative culture based on the core values we share across the group: ownership, accountability, innovation, adaptability and customer focus.

What you’ll have to do: 

• Lead and coordinate all legal and compliance activities of the company, including managing high-performing legal and compliance team;
• Drive legal strategy aligned with business objectives and growth plans;
• Champion compliance culture throughout the organization;
• Partner with product teams to enable innovative financial solutions by providing legal assistance in developing new product concepts;
• Collaborate with all divisions and departments to ensure compliance with regulations;
• Actively manage relationships with local regulators and industry associations;
• Issue opinions regarding the design of standard contractual documentation and other documents with legal specificity (norms, procedures and other documents for the financial products in the portfolio);
• Follow the national and European legislative changes, to update the characteristics of the products and to signal the corresponding changes in flow/procedures;
• Ensure the secretariat of the meetings of the General Meeting of Shareholders/Board of Directors or other management bodies;
• Ensure the representation and support of the company's interests in conciliations, before the courts at all levels as well as in relations with public authorities;
• Become a legal lead for financial services within the eMAG Group.

What Will You Bring to the Table? 

• University law degree;
• At least 5-7 years of experience in the financial-banking field (bank, fintech or law firm with experience working for clients from financial sector);
• Knowledge of financial services’ regulatory landscape, payments, consumer financial products and services, digital channels covering:
• eMoney and Payment Services: deep understanding of PSD2, electronic payment frameworks and practical business models implementing PSD2 frameworks;
• Credit Services: deep understanding of legal framework for offering consumer credit and merchant lending products;
• AML/CTF Compliance: knowledge of Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing regulations;
• Consumer Protection: experience with financial services regulations and consumer contracts;
• Data Protection: understanding of GDPR compliance and data privacy frameworks;
• Regulatory Relations: ability to build and manage relationships with supervisory and control authorities;
• International Sanctions: knowledge of sanctions laws and implementation procedures;
• Fluent in English;
• Experience with digital and e-commerce financial products is a plus;
• Proven experience advising financial institutions on contracts with consumers, entrepreneurs and external service providers/vendors;
• Entrepreneurial and results-oriented, with the ability to identify opportunities and drive business impact;
• Strong ownership mindset, combining accountability, adaptability, and sound risk-based decision-making;
• Innovation-focused, leveraging technology and RegTech solutions to address business and regulatory challenges;
• Excellent communication, planning, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders and deliver outcomes.

